---
// Interview Nudge privacy policy.
// Served at https://estlopacu.github.io/interview-nudge/privacy/
// Source of truth: interview-nudge repo → store/privacy-policy.md. Keep in sync.
import '../../styles/global.css';

const updated = 'November 11, 2026';
const email = 'estlopacu@gmail.com';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="terminal">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <title>Interview Nudge — Privacy Policy</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the Interview Nudge Android app. No data collected, no data shared." />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://estlopacu.github.io/interview-nudge/privacy/" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="policy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__muted">// </span>nudge:~$ cat privacy.md</p>
      <h1>Interview Nudge: Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        Interview Nudge ("the app") is a study tool that sends you local notifications with
        interview concepts. This policy explains what the app does with your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p class="callout">
        <strong>The app does not collect, transmit, sell or share any personal data.</strong>
        Everything you create stays on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>The app keeps the following in a local database on your phone:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Topics and concepts you create or edit, and the built-in sample concepts.</li>
        <li>Your notification settings: times per day, active hours, days, sound.</li>
        <li>A small local log of notification events (scheduled, shown, tapped), used to rotate concepts and avoid repeats.</li>
        <li>Your theme preference (light, dark or system).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data never leaves your device. The app has no account system, no server and no
        internet connection of its own. Uninstalling the app or clearing its storage deletes all of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Notifications</strong>: to show concept reminders. You can turn this off at any time in your phone's settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Alarms &amp; reminders (exact alarms)</strong>: optional; lets reminders arrive at the exact times you pick instead of being delayed by the system.</li>
        <li><strong>Run after restart / in background</strong>: to keep upcoming reminders scheduled after a reboot or when the app has not been opened for a while.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        If you tap <strong>Share</strong> on a concept, the app opens your phone's standard share
        sheet. Whatever you share, and with whom, is your choice and goes through the app you pick;
        Interview Nudge does not see or store it.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, ads and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The app contains no analytics, advertising, tracking or crash-reporting SDKs, and does not
        share data with third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The app is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from anyone.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this same address with a new
        "Last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>

      <p class="back"><a href="/">← estlopacu.github.io</a></p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  body {
    background: var(--surface-page);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .policy {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 20px 80px;
    color: var(--text-body);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-terminal);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .eyebrow__muted {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .meta {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    margin: 4px 0 32px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px);
    color: var(--text-strong);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text-strong);
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 40px 0 8px;
    padding-top: 4px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .callout {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-brand);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand) 8%, transparent);
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .callout strong {
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--text-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  a:hover {
    color: var(--brand-bright);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  .back {
    margin-top: 56px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 24px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .policy {
      padding: 40px 16px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
